# Module: ConfirmedEditAll

## ConfirmedEditAll-UC1 — Edit Enrollment Data

- Primary Actor(s): User
- Secondary Actor(s): System
- Trigger: User wants to edit enrollment data.
- Description: The system allows the user to edit fields within the enrollment data grid.
- Preconditions: User has necessary permissions. The session is valid. The screen is not set to read-only.
- Postconditions: Enrollment data is updated based on user input.
- Main Success Scenario:
  1. User accesses the enrollment data grid.
  2. User modifies fields such as actual hours and notes.
  3. User saves the changes.
  4. System updates the enrollment data and confirms no warnings.
- Extensions:
  - If data is not dirty, no update is made.
- Exceptions:
  - If fields are read-only, editing is not allowed.
  - If session is invalid, actions are canceled.
- Business Rules:
  - Only non-waived, non-graduated, non-inactive enrollments are editable.
  - Read-only fields prevent editing.
- Assumptions:
  - User has permission to edit.
- Open Issues:
  - None

## ConfirmedEditAll-UC2 — Save All Edits

- Primary Actor(s): User
- Secondary Actor(s): System
- Trigger: User opts to save all edits at once.
- Description: A command to save all changes made to the enrollment data simultaneously.
- Preconditions: User is in edit mode. Changes have been made to at least one field.
- Postconditions: All edited changes are saved.
- Main Success Scenario:
  1. User selects "Save All" from the interface.
  2. System saves all changes in the grid.
  3. User is redirected to confirm or return to the enrollment list.
- Extensions:
  - If no changes are detected, no save operation occurs.
- Exceptions:
  - System warns the user if any field validations fail.
- Business Rules:
  - All dirty fields must be identified and saved.
- Assumptions:
  - Edits are complete and valid.
- Open Issues:
  - None

## ConfirmedEditAll-UC3 — Navigate Next After Saving

- Primary Actor(s): User
- Secondary Actor(s): System
- Trigger: User saves current edits and proceeds to the next set of records.
- Description: User saves current changes and moves to edit the next batch of records.
- Preconditions: User is in edit mode, and changes have been made.
- Postconditions: Changes are saved, and the user sees the next records ready for editing.
- Main Success Scenario:
  1. User selects "Save Edit Next".
  2. System saves current changes.
  3. User is redirected to the next set of enrollment records for editing.
- Extensions:
  - None
- Exceptions:
  - Navigating to the next set fails if save operation reports errors.
- Business Rules:
  - Save and navigation occur only if there are no warnings.
- Assumptions:
  - User requests next set immediately after current save.
- Open Issues:
  - None

No additional use cases found.